message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on Can-Am Defender UTVs. Such vehicles are usually classified in 8704.21 or 8704.31 (dumpers/trucks) or 8703.21/8703.22/8703.23 (passenger vehicles). Because these are designed for goods transport with cargo boxes, a recent CBP ruling might place them in 8704. Engine sizes of 999 cc and 976 cc are both under 1,000 cc? 999 is under 1,000 and 976 is under 1,000, so the cylinder capacity falls under 8703.21 (not exceeding 1,000 cc), which is "Other" 8703.21.0100 or 8703.21.0140. But the question is whether they are 8704 or 8703.

The Defender is usually classified as an 8704 vehicle if it is principally designed for goods transport. Under 8704, spark-ignition engine vehicles with a GVW not exceeding 5 tonnes fall under 8704.31. The 8704.31 subheadings are 8704.31.0100 for "Other" within 8704.31, and 8704.31.0120 or similar for statistical breakdowns. Note that the 6x6 and Max seat 6 passengers. CBP rulings in the past (e.g., for the Polaris Ranger) put UTVs in 8704.31.0160, "Other: Other". The 8704.31 statistical suffixes: 8704.31.0160 is "Other" (with 8704.31.0120 "Chassis"? uncertain). I'll go with 8704.31.0160.

{"hts_code": "8704.31.0160", "reason": "Off-road utility vehicles with spark-ignition engines and tilting cargo boxes principally designed for transporting goods (GVW ≤5 t) are classified as motor vehicles for the transport of goods under heading 8704, subheading 8704.31."}
